WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.710
Anyone can build their own AI assistant, their own Jarvis.

2
00:00:02.760 --> 00:00:04.090
Here's how. It's simple.

3
00:00:04.140 --> 00:00:06.630
It fits in about 3000 lines and four text files.

4
00:00:06.680 --> 00:00:08.410
It's not magic. It's a loop.

5
00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:12.200
Every agent, from the simplest to the most expensive, has the same seven parts.

6
00:00:12.531 --> 00:00:14.011
a door, a heart,

7
00:00:14.011 --> 00:00:15.391
an identity, a brain,

8
00:00:15.391 --> 00:00:16.591
a memory, hands,

9
00:00:16.591 --> 00:00:17.091
and a vault.

10
00:00:17.091 --> 00:00:18.451
In this video,

11
00:00:18.451 --> 00:00:19.611
I’ll open up INTELECTO,

12
00:00:19.611 --> 00:00:21.511
the personal assistant we designed from scratch,

13
00:00:21.511 --> 00:00:22.811
and show you what each part does

14
00:00:22.811 --> 00:00:23.751
and where it lives.

15
00:00:23.751 --> 00:00:24.331
And at the end,

16
00:00:24.331 --> 00:00:25.391
I’ll tell you what’s coming in the

17
00:00:25.391 --> 00:00:26.991
next video: you’ll set up the files

18
00:00:26.991 --> 00:00:27.911
and install your own,

19
00:00:27.911 --> 00:00:29.101
step by step.

20
00:00:29.101 --> 00:00:31.031
INTELECTO is a personal AI assistant for

21
00:00:31.031 --> 00:00:31.771
one owner.

22
00:00:31.771 --> 00:00:33.631
It’s designed to run on your computer,

23
00:00:33.631 --> 00:00:35.011
talk with you through Telegram,

24
00:00:35.011 --> 00:00:35.991
remember what you say,

25
00:00:35.991 --> 00:00:37.531
and have the personality you write for

26
00:00:37.531 --> 00:00:37.911
it.

27
00:00:37.911 --> 00:00:39.751
What it isn’t matters just as much.

28
00:00:39.751 --> 00:00:40.911
It’s not multi-user,

29
00:00:40.911 --> 00:00:42.431
it doesn’t depend on the cloud,

30
00:00:42.431 --> 00:00:43.571
it doesn’t need Docker,

31
00:00:43.571 --> 00:00:44.831
it has no web dashboard,

32
00:00:44.831 --> 00:00:45.891
and it’s not a black box.

33
00:00:45.891 --> 00:00:48.271
The plan calls for seven dependencies and

34
00:00:48.271 --> 00:00:50.031
about three thousand lines you can read.

35
00:00:50.031 --> 00:00:52.211
It’s an antidote to bloated agent frameworks

36
00:00:52.211 --> 00:00:54.171
where nobody knows what’s running anymore.

37
00:00:54.171 --> 00:00:55.451
Before we look at the parts,

38
00:00:55.451 --> 00:00:57.311
here’s the full path a message takes.

39
00:00:57.311 --> 00:00:58.411
You write in Telegram.

40
00:00:58.411 --> 00:01:00.211
The channel receives it and passes it

41
00:01:00.211 --> 00:01:01.111
to the agent loop.

42
00:01:01.111 --> 00:01:02.731
The loop builds the context:

43
00:01:02.731 --> 00:01:03.751
who the agent is,

44
00:01:03.751 --> 00:01:04.471
who you are,

45
00:01:04.471 --> 00:01:05.871
and what it already knows about the

46
00:01:05.871 --> 00:01:06.291
topic.

47
00:01:06.291 --> 00:01:07.791
Then it sends everything to the AI

48
00:01:07.791 --> 00:01:08.331
model.

49
00:01:08.331 --> 00:01:09.851
If the model asks for a tool,

50
00:01:09.851 --> 00:01:11.111
the loop runs it and returns the

51
00:01:11.111 --> 00:01:11.471
result.

52
00:01:11.471 --> 00:01:13.051
When the model responds with text,

53
00:01:13.051 --> 00:01:14.611
the answer travels back through the channel

54
00:01:14.611 --> 00:01:15.561
to your phone.

55
00:01:15.561 --> 00:01:16.951
Seven parts, one path.

56
00:01:16.951 --> 00:01:18.251
Now, one by one.

57
00:01:18.251 --> 00:01:20.151
Part one: the channel,

58
00:01:20.151 --> 00:01:21.091
the way in.

59
00:01:21.091 --> 00:01:22.411
In the INTELECTO plan,

60
00:01:22.411 --> 00:01:24.151
that’s Telegram because it’s the simplest:

61
00:01:24.151 --> 00:01:25.631
one token and you’re set,

62
00:01:25.631 --> 00:01:27.311
with no public internet address.

63
00:01:27.311 --> 00:01:29.671
The agent keeps asking Telegram if a

64
00:01:29.671 --> 00:01:30.771
new message has arrived.

65
00:01:30.771 --> 00:01:32.484
If the reply is longer than four

66
00:01:32.484 --> 00:01:34.531
thousand characters, it splits it into several

67
00:01:34.531 --> 00:01:35.091
messages.

68
00:01:35.091 --> 00:01:37.171
And it shows that it’s typing while

69
00:01:37.171 --> 00:01:37.891
it thinks.

70
00:01:37.891 --> 00:01:39.591
The channel is a contract with three

71
00:01:39.591 --> 00:01:41.351
functions: start, send,

72
00:01:41.351 --> 00:01:42.091
and stop.

73
00:01:42.091 --> 00:01:43.911
Want WhatsApp, Discord,

74
00:01:43.911 --> 00:01:44.951
or Slack?

75
00:01:44.951 --> 00:01:46.811
That’s another file with the same contract,

76
00:01:46.811 --> 00:01:48.691
without changing anything else.

77
00:01:48.691 --> 00:01:50.071
Part two: the loop,

78
00:01:50.071 --> 00:01:51.131
the agent’s heart.

79
00:01:51.131 --> 00:01:52.711
This is where it stops being a

80
00:01:52.711 --> 00:01:53.411
chatbot.

81
00:01:53.411 --> 00:01:54.991
It receives the message,

82
00:01:54.991 --> 00:01:57.111
thinks, uses a tool if needed,

83
00:01:57.111 --> 00:01:57.951
checks the result,

84
00:01:57.951 --> 00:02:00.251
and thinks again until it responds with

85
00:02:00.251 --> 00:02:00.891
text.

86
00:02:00.891 --> 00:02:01.771
There’s a brake:

87
00:02:01.771 --> 00:02:03.771
at most five tool rounds per message.

88
00:02:03.771 --> 00:02:05.551
After that, it has to respond.

89
00:02:05.551 --> 00:02:06.631
Without this brake,

90
00:02:06.631 --> 00:02:08.051
an agent can keep spinning,

91
00:02:08.051 --> 00:02:09.631
spending money, and never finish.

92
00:02:09.631 --> 00:02:12.791
A short, readable loop with a limit:

93
00:02:12.791 --> 00:02:15.031
that’s what separates an agent from a

94
00:02:15.031 --> 00:02:15.831
conversation.

95
00:02:15.831 --> 00:02:17.491
Part three: the identity.

96
00:02:17.491 --> 00:02:18.971
This is the part you’ll change the

97
00:02:18.971 --> 00:02:19.471
most.

98
00:02:19.471 --> 00:02:21.231
It’s four plain text files in a

99
00:02:21.231 --> 00:02:22.571
folder called workspace.

100
00:02:22.571 --> 00:02:24.771
Soul is the assistant’s personality,

101
00:02:24.771 --> 00:02:26.371
tone, and values.

102
00:02:26.371 --> 00:02:28.511
Agents contains the behavior rules:

103
00:02:28.511 --> 00:02:30.011
check memory before answering,

104
00:02:30.011 --> 00:02:31.131
ask when unsure,

105
00:02:31.131 --> 00:02:33.111
refuse dangerous commands.

106
00:02:33.111 --> 00:02:34.511
User is your profile:

107
00:02:34.511 --> 00:02:35.931
how you like your answers and what

108
00:02:35.931 --> 00:02:36.731
language you use.

109
00:02:36.731 --> 00:02:38.851
And Memory contains the starting facts.

110
00:02:38.851 --> 00:02:39.851
With every message,

111
00:02:39.851 --> 00:02:41.311
the agent reads all four and builds

112
00:02:41.311 --> 00:02:42.371
the prompt for the model.

113
00:02:42.371 --> 00:02:43.391
Change the text,

114
00:02:43.391 --> 00:02:44.171
change the assistant,

115
00:02:44.171 --> 00:02:45.951
without writing any code.

116
00:02:45.951 --> 00:02:47.111
Part four: the brain,

117
00:02:47.111 --> 00:02:48.491
the AI model.

118
00:02:48.491 --> 00:02:49.991
INTELECTO works with two kinds.

119
00:02:49.991 --> 00:02:50.751
In the cloud,

120
00:02:50.751 --> 00:02:52.771
there’s OpenRouter: one key gives you access

121
00:02:52.771 --> 00:02:53.891
to more than a hundred models,

122
00:02:53.891 --> 00:02:56.091
from Claude and GPT to DeepSeek.

123
00:02:56.091 --> 00:02:57.211
On your computer,

124
00:02:57.211 --> 00:02:59.091
there’s Ollama: the model runs locally,

125
00:02:59.091 --> 00:03:01.151
with no per-message cost and nothing sent

126
00:03:01.151 --> 00:03:02.171
outside your computer.

127
00:03:02.171 --> 00:03:03.271
You can use both:

128
00:03:03.271 --> 00:03:04.411
the cloud for power,

129
00:03:04.411 --> 00:03:05.371
local for privacy.

130
00:03:05.371 --> 00:03:07.751
And switching brains doesn’t change anything else,

131
00:03:07.751 --> 00:03:09.991
because the provider is also a contract:

132
00:03:09.991 --> 00:03:11.831
it receives the conversation and tools,

133
00:03:11.831 --> 00:03:13.291
then returns the response.

134
00:03:13.591 --> 00:03:14.671
Part five: memory.

135
00:03:14.671 --> 00:03:16.351
It’s the difference between an AI that

136
00:03:16.351 --> 00:03:18.331
forgets everything when it restarts and one

137
00:03:18.331 --> 00:03:19.721
that’s known you for months.

138
00:03:19.721 --> 00:03:21.451
INTELECTO stores things in a database on

139
00:03:21.451 --> 00:03:22.091
your own computer,

140
00:03:22.091 --> 00:03:23.331
with keyword search.

141
00:03:23.331 --> 00:03:25.351
No API cost and no extra model,

142
00:03:25.351 --> 00:03:26.731
and that covers most of what you

143
00:03:26.731 --> 00:03:27.371
need to remember.

144
00:03:27.371 --> 00:03:28.671
Each memory has a category:

145
00:03:28.671 --> 00:03:29.651
a fact about you,

146
00:03:29.651 --> 00:03:30.771
a conversation summary,

147
00:03:30.771 --> 00:03:32.151
or a solution that worked.

148
00:03:32.151 --> 00:03:33.738
If a new memory is more than

149
00:03:33.738 --> 00:03:34.891
eighty percent like an old one,

150
00:03:34.891 --> 00:03:36.431
it updates it instead of making a

151
00:03:36.431 --> 00:03:36.911
duplicate.

152
00:03:36.911 --> 00:03:38.171
And with every message,

153
00:03:38.171 --> 00:03:39.991
it searches for what’s relevant and adds

154
00:03:39.991 --> 00:03:40.631
it to the context.

155
00:03:40.631 --> 00:03:41.651
Part

156
00:03:41.651 --> 00:03:42.751
six: the tools,

157
00:03:42.751 --> 00:03:43.791
the agent’s hands.

158
00:03:43.791 --> 00:03:45.371
Without them, it only chats.

159
00:03:45.371 --> 00:03:47.031
With them, it gets things done.

160
00:03:47.031 --> 00:03:48.731
The core includes reading a file,

161
00:03:48.731 --> 00:03:49.671
writing a file,

162
00:03:49.671 --> 00:03:50.791
listing a folder,

163
00:03:50.791 --> 00:03:51.811
running a command,

164
00:03:51.811 --> 00:03:53.431
and saving and searching memory.

165
00:03:53.431 --> 00:03:55.111
Each tool describes itself:

166
00:03:55.111 --> 00:03:56.891
its name, what it does,

167
00:03:56.891 --> 00:03:58.831
and which parameters it accepts.

168
00:03:58.831 --> 00:04:00.871
The model reads that description to decide

169
00:04:00.871 --> 00:04:01.711
whether to use it.

170
00:04:01.711 --> 00:04:02.731
Want a calendar,

171
00:04:02.731 --> 00:04:03.911
GitHub, or Notion?

172
00:04:03.911 --> 00:04:05.391
That’s a new file that follows the

173
00:04:05.391 --> 00:04:06.111
same pattern.

174
00:04:06.111 --> 00:04:07.691
The registry finds the tool on its

175
00:04:07.691 --> 00:04:10.111
own, without you changing the core.

176
00:04:10.111 --> 00:04:11.931
Part seven: the vault.

177
00:04:11.931 --> 00:04:13.971
An agent with hands needs limits.

178
00:04:13.971 --> 00:04:15.971
API keys are encrypted and tied to

179
00:04:15.971 --> 00:04:16.871
the machine’s hardware,

180
00:04:16.871 --> 00:04:18.471
so if someone steals the file,

181
00:04:18.471 --> 00:04:19.451
they can’t read them.

182
00:04:19.451 --> 00:04:21.371
Every command goes through a blocklist:

183
00:04:21.371 --> 00:04:22.671
commands to delete everything,

184
00:04:22.671 --> 00:04:23.491
format a disk,

185
00:04:23.491 --> 00:04:24.931
or restart don’t even run.

186
00:04:24.931 --> 00:04:26.971
Each command has a sixty-second time limit.

187
00:04:26.971 --> 00:04:28.891
And everything it runs is recorded in

188
00:04:28.891 --> 00:04:29.671
an audit log.

189
00:04:29.671 --> 00:04:31.111
You know what your agent did,

190
00:04:31.111 --> 00:04:32.011
when it did it,

191
00:04:32.011 --> 00:04:33.551
and which command it used.

192
00:04:33.551 --> 00:04:34.991
Now, here’s the idea that holds the

193
00:04:34.991 --> 00:04:36.271
seven parts together:

194
00:04:36.271 --> 00:04:36.811
contracts.

195
00:04:36.811 --> 00:04:38.531
Each part is defined by an interface,

196
00:04:38.531 --> 00:04:40.631
and you can swap out its implementation.

197
00:04:40.631 --> 00:04:42.051
Switch Telegram for WhatsApp,

198
00:04:42.051 --> 00:04:43.311
OpenRouter for Ollama,

199
00:04:43.311 --> 00:04:45.071
or one memory system for another,

200
00:04:45.071 --> 00:04:46.611
without rewriting the agent.

201
00:04:46.611 --> 00:04:47.771
And how was it built?

202
00:04:47.771 --> 00:04:49.271
First, the grocery store:

203
00:04:49.271 --> 00:04:51.651
a page that compares frameworks like OpenClaw,

204
00:04:51.651 --> 00:04:52.991
NanoBot, and Hermes,

205
00:04:52.991 --> 00:04:54.571
where you choose the ingredients.

206
00:04:54.571 --> 00:04:56.791
Those choices become a specification document.

207
00:04:56.791 --> 00:04:58.011
You give it to Claude Code with

208
00:04:58.011 --> 00:04:59.871
one sentence: read this and build it.

209
00:04:59.871 --> 00:05:01.731
The Jarvis example in the repository came

210
00:05:01.731 --> 00:05:03.531
from this process and passes all nine

211
00:05:03.531 --> 00:05:04.031
tests.

212
00:05:04.031 --> 00:05:05.291
And how do you build it out?

213
00:05:05.291 --> 00:05:07.291
The feature guide organizes everything into eight

214
00:05:07.291 --> 00:05:09.251
aisles: identity, security,

215
00:05:09.251 --> 00:05:11.191
channels, memory, automation,

216
00:05:11.191 --> 00:05:13.251
integrations, skills, and architecture.

217
00:05:13.251 --> 00:05:15.611
Today, the core covers the essentials.

218
00:05:15.611 --> 00:05:17.531
Scheduling, like sending a summary every Monday

219
00:05:17.531 --> 00:05:19.191
at nine, and web search are planned

220
00:05:19.191 --> 00:05:20.191
for the next phase.

221
00:05:20.191 --> 00:05:22.251
Each aisle shows what other frameworks offer

222
00:05:22.251 --> 00:05:24.131
and which INTELECTO files to change.

223
00:05:24.131 --> 00:05:25.291
You don’t need everything.

224
00:05:25.291 --> 00:05:26.811
Choose what helps with your day.

225
00:05:26.811 --> 00:05:28.991
Let’s recap: every agent has seven parts.

226
00:05:28.991 --> 00:05:30.111
The door, which is the channel.

227
00:05:30.111 --> 00:05:31.431
The heart, which is the loop with

228
00:05:31.431 --> 00:05:31.891
a brake.

229
00:05:31.891 --> 00:05:33.711
The identity, in four text files.

230
00:05:33.711 --> 00:05:35.611
The brain, in the cloud or locally.

231
00:05:35.611 --> 00:05:37.311
Memory, tools, and the vault.

232
00:05:37.311 --> 00:05:38.311
In the next video,

233
00:05:38.311 --> 00:05:39.411
we’ll get hands-on:

234
00:05:39.411 --> 00:05:40.531
set up the files,

235
00:05:40.531 --> 00:05:42.431
write the personality and profile for your

236
00:05:42.431 --> 00:05:44.511
assistant, create the bot in Telegram,

237
00:05:44.511 --> 00:05:45.511
choose the brain,

238
00:05:45.511 --> 00:05:47.251
then build and install it step by

239
00:05:47.251 --> 00:05:48.771
step, all the way to your first

240
00:05:48.771 --> 00:05:49.211
message.

241
00:05:49.211 --> 00:05:50.091
In the meantime,

242
00:05:50.091 --> 00:05:51.651
you can find INTELECTO at INEMA dot

243
00:05:51.651 --> 00:05:53.511
club, in the Beginner’s Learning Path.

244
00:05:53.511 --> 00:05:54.951
See you in the next video.

